From ede652c2afff2c1ff9d8f59907493e6b487c362f
Subject: wasm_threaded_loader: cancel in-flight loads on handle drop
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/ede652c2afff2c1ff9d8f59907493e6b487c362f
Date: 2026-05-16T13:17:06+01:00

Worker-side load tasks (spawn_local) previously had no cancellation path:
the AssetServer task on the main thread was the only Drop-tracked handle,
and even that runs to completion on wasm because Task<T> wraps an
uncancellable wasm_bindgen_futures::spawn_local future. Result: when all
strong handles to an in-flight asset dropped (scene change, realm switch),
the worker's reqwest fetch continued, holding the IPFS semaphore permit
until natural completion and starving the new scene's loads.

Race the worker's load_with_meta_and_loader_internal against a 2s poll of
AssetInfos::path_to_id. When process_handle_drop_internal has removed the
entry (no strong handles left), the cancel branch returns Err(LoadCancelled),
FutureExt::or drops the work future, and reqwest's AbortGuard aborts the
JS fetch on the way out, releasing the permit.
---
diff --git a/crates/bevy_asset/Cargo.toml b/crates/bevy_asset/Cargo.toml
